1	//! `reframe_clip {follow: "layout"}` — a camera and the screen behind it
2	//! re-laid on the current canvas (road map "creator-jobs" VR5b, spec §11
3	//! VR-53). Each switch Clip ▸ Camera Layout ▸ made is recognised on the
4	//! AUTHORED canvas (`from`, `layout_recognise.rs`) and solved again here by
5	//! `switch_layout`'s own composition (`compose_switch`), so a re-laid switch
6	//! is exactly the one a person would make on this canvas.
7	//!
8	//! - **The group.** Every top-level clip holding a layout action
9	//!   (`is_layout`) is laid out. A camera action at absolute T pairs with the
10	//!   layout action starting at T on the front-most track behind the
11	//!   camera's that holds one (CO-64's front and behind); a laid-out clip is
12	//!   a SCREEN when one on a track in front holds a layout action starting
13	//!   when one of its own does, else a CAMERA. The group is the closure over
14	//!   pairing from the given clip, plus each switch's PIECES: the clips of the
15	//!   same source (`same_source`, which ignores `in`) on a role's track
16	//!   starting after its action and before the track's next layout action,
17	//!   whose base is `alike` that action's end — the cut pieces of a laid-out
18	//!   recording, which CO-61's reach gave the layout as their base.
19	//! - **The replay.** Every group clip and piece takes `keep`'s per-axis
20	//!   rescale of its BASE (`rescale_video`); the group's layout actions are
21	//!   removed; the switches are composed again in time order at the camera
22	//!   action's absolute start, with [`switch_timing`]'s duration and curve,
23	//!   the recognised layout (Side by Side as Stacked on a canvas taller than
24	//!   wide) and its pieces as each role's later clips, nothing ending a
25	//!   reach. The focus is the old crop's centre (`focus_of`).
26	//! - **The other moves.** Each other moving end of a group clip or piece (a
27	//!   zoom) is re-based by [`conjugate`] from the placement in effect at its
28	//!   start on the old project to the one on the new, so what it zooms on
29	//!   keeps its place in the picture.
30	//!
31	//! Refused in VR-53 (c)'s order (`edit.rs`'s row); CO-62's refusals are not
32	//! asked again: each switch passed them when it was made.
33	
