1	//! `switch_layout` — a camera clip and the screen behind it laid out at the
2	//! playhead (road map "creator-jobs" CO6, spec §11 CO-61, CO-62, CO-64).
3	//! One op, so Clip ▸ Camera Layout ▸ is one undo step, "Camera Layout".
4	//! The geometry is `layout.rs`'s; this file is who is laid out, how far,
5	//! and what refuses.
6	//!
7	//! - **The roles** (CO-64): the camera, playing at `at` with a picture; the
8	//!   screen given (on a track behind) or found — the clip playing at `at`
9	//!   on the front-most visible, non-matte track behind the camera's with a
10	//!   drawn picture. No screen refuses `side_by_side` and `stacked`; the
11	//!   other three lay out the camera alone.
12	//! - **The switch** (CO-61): per role, the clip under `at` gets a LAYOUT
13	//!   ACTION (all six placement keys) at clip time `at − start`, 0.5 s and
14	//!   `ease_in_out` unless told, clamped to the clip and to its next later
15	//!   layout action, at least one frame; at its first frame the layout is
16	//!   its base and a one-frame layout action ends there (a cut). A layout
17	//!   action starting at `at` is replaced; one running at `at` is shortened
18	//!   to end there. The REACH (`edit_layout_reach.rs`) gives every later
19	//!   picture clip on the role's track starting before the next layout
20	//!   action, `through` or the track's end the layout as its base.
21	//! - **The refusals** (CO-62), in order: the camera, the screen, a nest
22	//!   clip asked for a radius it cannot draw, a mover — a non-layout action
23	//!   that moves a role clip and ends after `at` (a full-placement screen
24	//!   exempt in the three layouts that leave it full) — then whatever the
25	//!   composed ops say. `nest: true` nests the moving role's clips first and
26	//!   lays out the nest clip, unless one of them is already laid out.
27	//!
28	//! Composed from `remove_action`, `set_action`, `add_action`,
29	//! `set_action_end`, `set_video` and `nest_clips`, each refusal inherited in
30	//! its own words.
